"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif; text-align: center;\" align=\"center\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">&gt;&nbsp;20%</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 155.95pt; background: #daeef3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"208\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif; text-align: center;\" align=\"center\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">&gt;&nbsp;20</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 474.9pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" colspan=\"4\" width=\"633\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><strong><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Poorly differentiated PanNENs: pancreatic neuroendocrine carcinomas (PanNECs)</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 163.05pt; background: #daeef3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" colspan=\"2\" width=\"217\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">PanNEC (G3)</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 155.9pt; background: #daeef3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"208\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif; text-align: center;\" align=\"center\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">&gt;&nbsp;20%</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 155.95pt; background: #daeef3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"208\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif; text-align: center;\" align=\"center\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">&gt;&nbsp;20</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 21.3pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"28\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">&nbsp;</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 5cm; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"189\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Small cell type</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 155.9pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"208\">&nbsp;</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 155.95pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"208\">&nbsp;</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 21.3pt; background: #daeef3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"28\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">&nbsp;</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 5cm; background: #daeef3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"189\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Large cell type</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 155.9pt; background: #daeef3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"208\">&nbsp;</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 155.95pt; background: #daeef3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"208\">&nbsp;</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 474.9pt; border-top: none; border-right: none; border-left: none; border-image: initial; border-bottom: 1pt solid windowtext; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" colspan=\"4\" width=\"633\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><strong><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Mixed neuroendocrine&ndash;non-neuroendocrine neoplasm (MiNEN)</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><sup><span lang=\"EN-GB\">a</span></sup><span lang=\"EN-GB\">The</span><span lang=\"EN-GB\"> Ki-67 proliferation index is based on the evaluation of &ge;&nbsp;500&nbsp;cells in areas of higher nuclear labelling (hotspots). The mitotic count is based on the evaluation of mitoses in 50&nbsp;HPF (0.2&nbsp;mm<sup>2</sup> each) in areas of higher density and is expressed as the number of mitoses per 10&nbsp;HPF (2.0&nbsp;mm<sup>2</sup>). The final grade is determined on the basis of whichever index (Ki-67 or mitotic) places the tumour in the highest grade category. For assessing Ki-67, casual visual estimation (eyeballing) is not recommended; manual counting using printed images is advocated instead </span><span class=\"Ref-PMID\" style=\"color: #984806; background: #ccc0d9;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">{25412850}</span></span><span lang=\"EN-GB\">.</span></p>",
